  "street_name": "GALPINS ROAD",
  "decision_date": "02/10/2025",
  "date_building_work_completed_under_previous_permission": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - By reason of the plot subdivision, height, proximity to the boundary, scale, form and approach to the dwelling indicatively shown, the proposed development would result in material harm to the character and appearance of the locality, in conflict with London Plan policies D3 and D4 and Policy D12.3 of the Local Plan.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed development, by reason of the indicative bulk, massing, proximity to the shared boundary and height, would result in material harm to the amenities of the occupiers of 251-255 Galpins Road by way of unreasonable sense of enclosure and overbearing form, contrary to London Plan policy D6 and Local Plan policies D12.2, D12.3 and D12.4.",
    "Reason : 3 - By reason of unsatisfactory layout, the scheme results in an intensification of use of the side access, with an associated adverse impact in terms of noise and disturbance to the detriment of the residential amenity of neighbouring occupants, in particular, no. 255 and 257 Galpins Road.  Additionally, in the absence of information relating to the specification of the proposed ASHP, the applicant has failed to demonstrate that the impact on these adjoining properties, by way of noise disturbance, would be acceptable. The scheme is contrary to London Plan policy D6 and Local Plan policies D12.2, D12.3 and D12.4",
    "Reason : 4 - In the absence of a legal agreement to secure the required carbon offset financial contribution of �2,242.80, the submission has failed to adequately mitigate for its impact on climate change and has failed to demonstrate compliance with policies SI 2 of the London Plan 2021 and Policies CC2.1 - CC2.6 of the Local Plan 2024.",
    "Reason : 5 - The proposed development, by reason of the means of access and position of proposed cycle and bin storage, results in substandard refuse and cycle provision. In addition, the removal of rear access to the host dwelling, removes the potential for cycle parking in the rear garden or outbuilding of the host dwelling. The proposal fails to meet the relevant standards of accessible and inclusive design, would not create an adequate standard of accommodation and would not create cycle parking facilities in accordance with the London Cycling Design Standards, in conflict with policies D6, T1, T5 and T7 of the London Plan and policies D12.3, T16.2 and T16.3 of the Local Plan.",
    "Reason : 6 - In the absence of a s.106 legal agreement or other legal mechanism to secure the construction of the proposed development as a self-build/custom build development, the applicant has failed to ensure that the proposed development benefits from BNG exemption, contrary to Policy G6 of the London Plan and Policy O15.3 of the Local Plan.",
    "Reason : 7 - By reason of the lack of adequate sustainable drainage details, the proposal is considered to conflict with London Plan Policies SI 13 and Local Plan policies F15.7.",
    "Reason : 8 - INFORMATIVE\r\nNote to Applicant\r\nIn accordance with paragraph 38 of the NPPF, The London Borough of Merton  (LBM) takes a positive and proactive approach to development proposals focused on solutions. LBM works with applicants/agents in a positive and proactive manner by:\r\n\"\tOffering a pre-application advice and duty desk service. \r\n\"\tWhere possible, suggesting solutions to secure a successful outcome.\r\n\"\tAs appropriate, updating applicants/agents of any issues that may arise in the processing of their application.\r\nIn this instance:\r\n\"\tThe application was not considered to comply with the provisions of the Development Plan and NPPF as submitted, and would have required substantial changes such that a new application would be required. \r\n\"\tIt is noted that the applicant/agent did not engage in any pre-application discussions.\r\n\"\tThe applicant is advised to seek pre-application advice on any resubmission.\r\n"
  ],
